Static app-icon entries, so the unix side gets every icon size.

macdrv_app_icon() passes its icon entries to the unix side with NtCallbackReturn(), and in an ARM64EC process only
the first entry of a stack array arrives intact. The callback runs once per process (pthread_once in set_app_icon).

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (a change to Wine).

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/dllmain.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/dllmain.c
@@ -254,7 +254,9 @@
  */
 static NTSTATUS WINAPI macdrv_app_icon(void *arg, ULONG size)
 {
-    struct app_icon_entry entries[64];
+    /* Static: NtCallbackReturn passes the unix side a pointer to these entries, and in an ARM64EC process only the
+       first entry of a stack array arrives intact. This runs once per process (pthread_once in set_app_icon). */
+    static struct app_icon_entry entries[64];
     HRSRC res_info;
     HGLOBAL res_data;
     GRPICONDIR *icon_dir;
